US Census government boundaries, TIGER/Line 2026

Source: U.S. Census Bureau, 2026 TIGER/Line Shapefiles, state-based Place and
County Subdivision files for the 50 states and DC. All legal boundaries and
names are as of January 1, 2026 (Boundary and Annexation Survey); released
2026-10-14. Downloaded 2026-11-05.
https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/TIGER2026/PLACE/
https://www2.census.gov/geo/tiger/TIGER2026/COUSUB/
https://www2.census.gov/geo/pdfs/maps-data/data/tiger/tgrshp2026/TGRSHP2026_TechDoc_Ch3.pdf
Only FUNCSTAT=A: active government providing primary general-purpose functions
(incorporated places MTFCC=G4110, county subdivisions MTFCC=G4040).
https://www.census.gov/library/reference/code-lists/functional-status-codes.html
State FIPS/postal abbreviations:
https://www2.census.gov/geo/docs/reference/state.txt

Public domain, a work of the United States government (17 USC 105).
The Census Bureau requests source citation. No Census endorsement is implied.

Modified: retained source-namespace/GEOID, state, NAMELSAD and full-resolution
polygon rings, rounded coordinates to 1e-7 degrees and delta-encoded each ring.
No geometric simplification. NAD83 coordinates are used without datum
transformation. All 35,611 selected entities were checked for completeness,
duplicate IDs and geometric validity (none invalid). Retained 35,611 entities in
50,051 polygon parts. The pinned gzip SHA256 is
706a593d0bdedb7a26c11078523bf95aa6a3681ebcda0ef090517d04b111cbce.

Census boundaries are statistical representations, not legal land descriptions
or a determination of jurisdictional authority or property ownership. Census
provides no positional-accuracy warranty; output precision is not surveyed
accuracy. The coordinate-encoding boundary guard does not bound source error.
This source excludes statistical CDPs, nonfunctioning entities and government
statuses other than A. It does not establish postal-city or community identity.
